  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National HIV/AIDS Programme, The Health Commission, under the Episcopal Conference of Malawi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">More specifically, the planned intervention focuses on strengthening the capacity of the ECM to respond appropriately. The objectives are to: 

&#xb7;	Identify the strengths and weaknesses of the health service delivery programme in the 7 diocese through monitoring and evaluating progress and recognise areas of need
&#xb7;	Based on the needs identified, to provide technical support to staff working in all ECM health units and home-based care services in order to improve the quality of service for people infected and affected by HIV/AIDS.
&#xb7;	To conduct refresher training courses for health tutors and patient attendants in order to update and strengthen their skills 
&#xb7;	To facilitate dialogue between the Church and communities on aspects of care and prevention of HIV and AIDS in all the dioceses in Malawi</narrative>
  </description>
